.Dd $Mdocdate: August 5 2026 $
.Dt OPENBAR.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openbar.conf
.Nd configuration file for openbar
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the configuration file for
.Xr openbar 1 .
It controls which system information is displayed on the
status bar.
.Pp
The file may be placed at
.Pa ~/.openbar.conf
.Pq per-user
or
.Pa /etc/openbar.conf
.Pq system-wide .
If both exist the per-user file takes precedence.
.Pp
A custom path may be specified with the
.Fl c
option of
.Xr openbar 1 .
.Sh SYNTAX
Each line is a
.Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value
pair.
Leading and trailing whitespace is ignored.
Empty lines and full lines whose first non-whitespace character is
.Sq #
are ignored.
Keys are matched exactly, and unknown keys produce a warning.
Boolean features accept
.Dq yes
or
.Dq no .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar logo
Displayed text or name.
Example:
.Dl logo=OpenBar
.It Ar date
Display the current date and time.
.It Ar cpu
Display CPU speed and temperature.
.It Ar bat
Display battery status and percentage.
.It Ar mem
Display free memory in MB.
.It Ar load
Display the 1-minute load average.
.It Ar net
Display public and private IP addresses.
Public addresses are fetched from
.Pa ifconfig.me
by a sandboxed network worker process.
.It Ar hostname
Display the system hostname.
.It Ar interface
Network interface used to obtain the internal IP address.
Example:
.Dl interface=iwm0
.It Ar vpn
Display whether a WireGuard
.Pq wg
interface is active.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.openbar.conf
Per-user configuration.
.It Pa /etc/openbar.conf
System-wide configuration.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
logo=openbar status
date=yes
cpu=yes
bat=no
mem=yes
load=yes
net=yes
hostname=yes
interface=iwm0
vpn=yes
.Ed
.Sh SECURITY
The enabled features directly affect the
.Xr pledge 2
promise set retained by the main process during
steady-state operation.
The normal set is
.Dq stdio unix ;
.Ar mem
adds the valid
.Dq vminfo
promise for
.Dv VM_UVMEXP .
.Ar vpn
or
.Ar net
adds
.Dq route
because
.Xr getifaddrs 3
uses
.Dv NET_RT_IFLIST .
CPU MHz is sampled before pledge, and
.Dv HW_SENSORS
is always allowed.
There are no generic
.Dq sysctl ,
.Dq ioctl
promises.
.Pp
The
.Dv APM_IOC_GETPOWER
operation used for battery updates is not available under any pledge promise.
For this reason,
.Ar bat Ns =yes
disables pledge in the display process with a warning, while its unveil policy
remains active.
.Pp
The network worker is forked only when
.Ar net
is enabled and runs under an independent sandbox with
.Dq stdio inet dns
and filesystem visibility limited to DNS resolution
files.
.Pp
The configuration is read before sandbox setup.
The display process unveils its X11 socket and X authority file; it also
unveils
.Pa /dev/apm
when required.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openbar 1 ,
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Xr unveil 2 ,
.Xr apm 4
